00:52:20.640 --> 00:52:23.340
efforts you lead.

00:52:23.340 --> 00:52:26.040
Gerard, I see your hand
went up on this topic.

00:52:26.040 --> 00:52:30.300
- Yeah. So when COVID
hit and everybody started working from

00:52:30.300 --> 00:52:32.820
home, what we did was--

00:52:32.820 --> 00:52:35.670
I establish tee time

00:52:35.670 --> 00:52:38.880
a couple of times a week for
the team to get together.

00:52:38.880 --> 00:52:40.800
And there was a
very simple rule--

00:52:40.800 --> 00:52:42.660
you were only asked to

00:52:42.660 --> 00:52:47.850
talk about work-related things
in the last five minutes.

00:52:47.850 --> 00:52:50.520
But it really helped to

00:52:50.520 --> 00:52:53.710
have that interpersonal connection with
the people in the team.

00:52:53.710 --> 00:52:58.020
And so you kind of knew if they
were stressed, if they were

00:52:58.020 --> 00:53:00.450
doing something fun
at home or whatever.

00:53:00.450 --> 00:53:02.310
And in of those last
couple of minutes,

00:53:02.310 --> 00:53:05.130
you could quickly ask
what they were working on,

00:53:05.130 --> 00:53:08.460
did anyone need any help,

00:53:08.460 --> 00:53:13.710
do we need to make
any connections between different teams.

00:53:13.710 --> 00:53:15.510
And so to

00:53:15.510 --> 00:53:17.510
Libby's point, yeah,

00:53:19.350 --> 00:53:24.600
if you don't force it,
those conversations don't happen. And

00:53:24.600 --> 00:53:26.310
because the first couple
of weeks of COVID,

00:53:26.310 --> 00:53:30.270
no one talked to each
other. Everybody was just doing work

00:53:30.270 --> 00:53:31.500
and

00:53:31.500 --> 00:53:33.790
that just didn't work.

00:53:33.790 --> 00:53:35.130
So

00:53:35.130 --> 00:53:38.400
after initiating that tea time

00:53:38.400 --> 00:53:41.520
that at least that
forced conversation

00:53:41.520 --> 00:53:44.280
really helped in multiple
ways, not just socially,

00:53:44.280 --> 00:53:47.430
but also in keeping
that collaboration and that

00:53:47.430 --> 00:53:49.430
networking going.

00:53:50.760 --> 00:53:54.900
- I'm thinking about how
sometimes we've talked about

00:53:54.900 --> 00:53:57.600
the power of

00:53:57.600 --> 00:54:01.950
automating something that was once
manual and how that helps

00:54:01.950 --> 00:54:05.250
you exponentially
down the road.

00:54:05.250 --> 00:54:08.070
But it's almost the same
with the community efforts.

00:54:08.070 --> 00:54:12.180
You need to take a chance to
step back and look at the big

00:54:12.180 --> 00:54:16.440
picture and create that
community so that it can help

00:54:16.440 --> 00:54:20.490
everybody later on down the
road and that you're not just

00:54:20.490 --> 00:54:24.840
the one person who everybody's
going to for questions

00:54:24.840 --> 00:54:28.500
and that there's so many
others that are supporting each other.

00:54:31.020 --> 00:54:34.090
Eugene, I see your
hand is raised too.

00:54:34.090 --> 00:54:36.940
- Yeah. I mean,

